==Hungarian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|hu|ohu|vagyon}}. See Hungarian {{m|hu|volt}}.
* Forms beginning with {{m|hu||v-}} are from {{der|hu|fiu-pro|-}} {{m|urj-pro|*wole-||to be}}. Cognate with {{cog|mns-nor|о̄луӈкве}}, {{cog|fi|olla}} and {{cog|et|olema}}. Compare inflected forms such as {{m|hu|volt}}, {{m|hu|volna}}, {{m|hu|való}} and Old Hungarian {{m|hu|vola}} or {{m|hu|vala}}. See also {{m|hu|vagy}} for the stem in present tense.<!-- result of palatalization: /vɒl/ > /vɒʎ/ > /vɒj/ > /vɒɟ/.-->

* Forms beginning with {{m|hu||l-}} are from {{der|hu|fiu-pro|-}} {{m|urj-pro|*le-||to become}}. Cognate with {{cog|fi|lienee|pos=potential of {{m|fi|olla}}}}, {{cog|krl|lienöy|pos=potential of {{m|krl|olla}}}}, {{cog|se|leat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hu-IPA}}
* {{audio|hu|Hu-van.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|hu|ɒn|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{hu-verb}}

# {{lb|hu|copulative}} to [[be]]
#: {{ant|hu|[[nem]]…}}
#: {{uxi|hu|Boldog '''vagyok'''.|I '''am''' happy.}}
# [[there be|there to be]], to [[exist]]
#: {{syn|hu|létezik|található}}
#: {{ant|hu|nincs}}
#: {{uxi|hu|'''Van''' itt valaki?|'''Is there''' anybody here?}}
# to [[have]]; someone ({{hu-case|nak}}) has something ({{m|hu|-a}}/{{m|hu|-e}}/{{m|hu|-ja}}/{{m|hu|-je}})
#: {{uxi|hu|Péter'''nek van''' egy kutyá'''ja'''.|Peter '''has''' a dog.}}
# to be [[make|made]] (out) of something {{gloss|with {{hu-case|ból}}}}
#: {{syn|hu|készült}}
#: {{uxi|hu|Ez az ajtó fá'''ból van'''.|This door '''is''' made '''out of wood'''.}}
# {{lb|hu|auxiliary|{{construed with|hu|[[-va]]/[[-ve]]}} (adverbial participle) of the main verb}} to [[be]] ({{non-gloss definition|indicating the [[statal]] [[passive]]}})
#: {{uxi|hu|A lakásom biztosít'''va van'''.|My apartment (flat) '''is (has been)''' insure'''d'''.|q=from {{m|hu||biztosítva}} ← {{m|hu|biztosít}}}}
#: {{uxi|hu|A probléma meg '''van''' old'''va'''.|The issue '''is (has been)''' solv'''ed'''.|q=from {{m|hu||megoldva}} ← {{m|hu|megold}}}}
#* {{quote-text|hu|year=1846|author=w:János Arany|title={{w|Toldi trilogy|Toldi}}|url=http://mek.oszk.hu/00500/00597/html/toldi02.htm#01_06|section=canto 6, stanza 13|translator=Anton N. Nyerges|sectionurl=https://mek.oszk.hu/00500/00595/html/epics2.htm#4
|passage=„Szakmány módra '''van''' rám mér'''ve''' minden óra: / Jöttem kegyelmedhez búcsuvevő szóra.”|t=“Every hour '''is''' measured as though by contract. / I come to bid you now farewell.”}}

====Usage notes====
The functions of this verb don’t fully overlap with the usage of corresponding verbs of other languages (compare {{noncog|es|ser}}, {{m|es|estar}} or {{noncog|th|คือ}}, {{m|th|เป็น}}, {{m|th|อยู่}}):
:* {{uxi|hu|'''Van''' egy [[törpe]] a [[zseb]]emben. &nbsp; ''or'' &nbsp; Törpe '''van''' a zsebemben. |'''There is''' a dwarf in my pocket.}} – {{smc|existence}} (used with an indefinite subject)
:* {{uxi|hu|[Nekem] '''van''' egy zsebtörpém.|'''I have''' a pocket-dwarf.|lit=[to me] '''there is''' a pocket-dwarf-my}} – {{smc|possession}} <!-- (it can also be seen as a subtype of the existential sense)-->
:* {{uxi|hu|A törpe a zsebemben '''van'''.|The dwarf '''is''' in my pocket.}} – {{smc|location}} (used with a prepositional phrase in English)
:* {{uxi|hu|A törpe jól '''van'''.|The dwarf '''is''' well.}} – {{smc|state, condition}} (used with an adverb in English)
:* {{uxi|hu|A törpe kicsi '''∅'''.|The dwarf '''is''' small.}} – {{smc|[[copula]]}} (used with an adjective or a noun as part of the predicate)
* As we can see, the verb is omitted in the last sentence. It happens only in the given sense and only in the present-tense third-person singular and plural forms (“he/she/it” and “they”):
*: When used with an adjective (qualification) or a noun (whether with the definite or the indefinite article), i.e. when it answers the question ''who?'' or ''what?'' (including ''what …… like?'') or ''which?'', the (indicative present third-person) forms ''van'' and ''vannak'' are omitted:
*:: {{uxi|hu|Béla okos.|Béla '''is''' clever.}}
*:: {{uxi|hu|Béla a király.|Béla '''is''' the king.}}
*:: {{uxi|hu|Béla egy ember.|Béla '''is''' a human.}}
*: On the other hand, if ''is'' or ''are'' answers the question ''where?'' or ''how?'', these verb forms will appear as usual:
*:: {{uxi|hu|Béla itt '''van'''.|Béla '''is''' here.}}
*:: {{uxi|hu|Béla jól '''van'''.|Béla '''is''' (feeling) well.}}
*: It also appears if ''van''/''vannak'' is the [[w:Hungarian grammar#Emphasis|focus]] of the sentence. This happens when the sentence means that the property described by the adjective (e.g. strength) reaches or exceeds some specified level and this is emphasized by the speaker. In this case, the adjective is preceded by a word like {{m|hu|olyan||such}}, {{m|hu|annyira||that much}}, {{m|hu|elég||enough}}.
*:: {{uxi|hu|Béla '''van''' annyira erős, hogy felemelje a szekrényt.|Béla '''is''' strong '''enough''' to lift the cupboard.}}
*: The forms other than ''van'' and ''vannak'' are always used.
*:: {{uxi|hu|Béla okos '''volt'''.|Béla '''was''' clever.}}
*:: {{uxi|hu|Okos '''vagyok'''.|I '''am''' clever.}}
*: In other senses, all forms are used:
*: With adverbs and [[w:adverbial participle|adverbial participles]] (suffixed ''{{m|hu|-va}}''/''{{m|hu|-ve}}'')
*:: {{uxi|hu|Hogy '''van'''?|How '''is''' he? (''also'' How '''are''' you?, ''formal singular'')}}
*:: {{uxi|hu|El '''van''' törve.|It '''is''' broken.}}

* The negative form is {{l|hu|nincs}} or {{l|hu|nincsen}} and {{l|hu|sincs}} or {{l|hu|sincsen}} (the latter two expressing “is not … either”).
*: {{uxi|hu|'''Nincs''' pénzem.|I '''don't have''' any money.}}
*: {{uxi|hu|Itt '''sincs''' étel.|There ''''isn’t''' any food here '''either'''.}}
* If the predicate includes an adjective or a noun, that is, if it answers the question ''who, what'' etc. (see above), the third person present forms are omitted again, only ''nem'' remains:
*: {{uxi|hu|Béla '''nem''' tanár.|Béla '''is not''' a teacher.}}

{{sense|exist, there is, to have}} (''have'' is expressed by ''there is'' in Hungarian):
*: {{uxi|hu|'''Van''' egy ház a hegyen.|'''There is''' a house on the mountain.}}
*: {{uxi|hu|'''Van''' egy kutyám.|I '''have''' a dog.|lit='''There is''' a dog-[of]-mine.}}

